{#- The research behind a case study: the sources (what was read, watched and
    seen), lines that carry them down into one frame, and in the frame the
    question they led to beside the key findings.

    Everything comes from the page's front matter, so any case study can have
    one:

      research:
        sources:      [{ title, image, alt?, url? }]   a source without a url is a photo of my own
        timeline:     [{ title, points[] }]             the steps taken, shown above the sources (optional)
        question:     the "how might we" the research led to
        figure:       { src, alt, width }               a picture under the question (optional)
        findings:     [{ title, detail? }]

    Included through the oneLine filter (Markdown ends raw HTML at a blank line):
      {% filter oneLine %}{% include "partials/study/research.njk" %}{% endfilter %}

    Without scripts the sources are a plain grid, each with its title and
    link. research.js gathers them into a pile that cycles, opens a source on
    hover, focus or a tap, and can be paused (styles: "Research" in style.css). -#}
{%- set r = research %}
{%- if r.timeline %}
<ol class="timeline">
  {%- for s in r.timeline %}
  <li class="timeline__step"><p class="timeline__t">{{ s.title }}</p>{% if s.points %}<ul class="timeline__list">{% for p in s.points %}<li>{{ p }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}</li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ol>
{%- endif %}
<div class="rw" data-cycle="{{ r.cycle or 4 }}">
  <ul class="rw__pile" role="list" aria-label="Research sources">
    {%- for s in r.sources %}
    <li class="rw__card" role="group" aria-label="{{ s.title }}">
      <span class="rw__thumb"><img src="{{ s.image }}" alt="{{ s.alt or '' }}" sizes="(max-width: 720px) 60vw, 300px"></span>
      <span class="rw__foot">
        <span class="rw__text"><span class="rw__title">{{ s.title }}</span>{% if s.url %}<span class="rw__host">{{ s.url | host }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
        {%- if s.url %}
        <a class="icon-link rw__link" href="{{ s.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open original source: {{ s.title }} (opens in a new tab)" title="Open source in a new tab"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11 4h5v5M16 4l-7 7M14 11v4a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H5a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V7a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h4"/></svg></a>
        {%- endif %}
      </span>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  <div class="rw__detail" hidden></div>
  <button type="button" class="btn rw__pause" hidden><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 4v12M13 4v12"/></svg><span>Pause motion</span></button>
  {% include "partials/study/flow.njk" %}
</div>
<div class="panel split">
  <div class="split__lead">
    <h3 class="question">{{ r.question }}</h3>
    {%- if r.figure %}
    <img class="question__fig" src="{{ r.figure.src }}" alt="{{ r.figure.alt or '' }}" style="--w: {{ r.figure.width or 248 }}" sizes="{{ r.figure.width or 248 }}px">
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="split__main">
    <p class="label">Key findings</p>
    <ol class="findings">
      {%- for f in r.findings %}
      <li class="finding"><span class="label">{{ "0" if loop.index < 10 }}{{ loop.index }}</span><div><p class="finding__t">{{ f.title }}</p>{% if f.detail %}<p class="caption">{{ f.detail }}</p>{% endif %}</div></li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>
